    "html": "<p class=\"doc-lede\">Non-equilibrium thermodynamics, informational entropy reversal, and chromatin architecture restoration. A protocol for projecting localized negentropic counter-currents across the genome–water–consciousness axis.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"card-grid cols-3 doc-index\">\n    <a class=\"card index-card\" href=\"#/protocol/holographic\" data-accent=\"teal\"><span class=\"index-num\">01</span><h3>Holographic Biophysics</h3><p>Entropic isomorphism from chromatin to cosmos, the thermodynamic definition of senescence, and the 18-6 dry-fasting baseline.</p></a>\n    <a class=\"card index-card\" href=\"#/protocol/protocol\" data-accent=\"amber\"><span class=\"index-num\">02</span><h3>Master Protocol</h3><p>Three synchronized delivery windows — awakening elixir, OMAD ketogenic meal, bedtime somatic reset — plus pulsed entheogenic strata.</p></a>\n    <a class=\"card index-card\" href=\"#/protocol/epigenetics\" data-accent=\"violet\"><span class=\"index-num\">03</span><h3>Epigenetic Repolymerization</h3><p>TET demethylation, Pol β gap resynthesis, thiol redox protection, the heterochromatin lock, and telomeric extension.</p></a>\n    <a class=\"card index-card\" href=\"#/protocol/matrix\" data-accent=\"blue\"><span class=\"index-num\">04</span><h3>Biophysics &amp; Shielding</h3><p>Exclusion-zone water, proton conduction, optical tuning, lipid shielding, inflammasome blockade, and the fascial matrix.</p></a>\n    <a class=\"card index-card\" href=\"#/protocol/meditation\" data-accent=\"rose\"><span class=\"index-num\">05</span><h3>Mind Recoding Engine</h3><p>A six-phase, thirty-minute meditation with selectable five-minute chapters and optional 40 Hz binaural audio.</p></a>\n    <a class=\"card index-card\" href=\"#/protocol/lexicon\" data-accent=\"green\"><span class=\"index-num\">06</span><h3>Lexicon</h3><p>A searchable master lexicon of formal mathematical formulas, biochemical pathways, and cosmological definitions.</p></a>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"card\" data-accent=\"violet\">\n    <h3 class=\"card-kicker\">The calendar the cadences are counted in</h3>\n    <p>Every cadence here — daily, weekly, monthly — is counted in the <a href=\"#/read/calendar-360\">360° symmetrical calendar</a>: twelve months of thirty days, five six-day weeks to a month, and a day lengthened so that 360 of them span one solar revolution exactly.</p>\n    <p>The arithmetic is why it is used. Every month is the same length and begins on the same weekday, so a monthly reset always falls the same distance from the weekly one and the two never drift apart. On the Gregorian grid a “monthly” cadence slides between 28 and 31 days and silently decouples from anything weekly; here the intervals nest — 6, 30, 360 — which is what makes a protocol built on phase relation schedulable at all.</p>\n    <p>The day itself is a true rotation of ordinary length — the calendar puts its remainder in five days outside the count rather than in the length of the day — so anything entrained to light keeps its real hour. The 18-hour window, the bedtime reset and the sleep architecture the third phase depends on sit on the solar day, and the 360° count governs the intervals between them.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"card\" data-accent=\"teal\">\n    <h3 class=\"card-title\">How to read this document</h3>\n    <p>Each section can be read on its own. Technical passages are followed, where useful, by a short passage <em>in plain terms</em> that carries the same idea in an everyday image. Formulas are rendered inline; tables scroll sideways on small screens. In the Master Protocol, a body-mass selector rescales every dose on the page.</p>\n  </div>"
